      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{4a-6b}{4}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4a-6b}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{4a}{4}-\\frac{6b}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{4}\\cdot a-\\frac{6}{4}\\cdot b & = \\\\ a-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot b & = \\\\ a-\\frac{3b}{2} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
